      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, internal defects like large voids caused by fungal rot, hidden concentrated compressive stress defects (Section 11A defects), or kinked fibers that aren't visible on the exterior surface are just as critical as knots. You must rely on the manufacturer's stamp and verified rating rather than visual inspection, as inertia tests are required to certify timber for specific loads. It is also vital to get the exact mill test report and grade stamp, ensuring the timber has been pressure-treated or protected since Oregon's damp climate can hide internal decay that compromises long-term structural integrity.",
