      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, experienced woodworkers definitely encounter that \"character\" where timber behaves unpredictably due to hidden shrinkage, moisture inconsistencies, or chemical treatments that alter its mechanical properties. Even with perfect grade stamps, variations in local knot size or end-grain condition can make a beam bend or twist more than the nominal rating suggests under real-world loads. To mitigate this, it is often safer to treat the wood as fully uncertain and add extra strength (like steel plates or a larger size) if the situation involves critical roof or floor spans.",
